          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Tuckahoe and Early Schooling",
          "content": "After his father's death, young Thomas studied at the Reverend James Maury's classical academy in Albemarle from 1758 to 1760. Maury drilled him in Latin, Greek, and French. Thomas memorized Homer and Virgil and absorbed an Anglican gentleman's curriculum. He later said Maury was a correct classical scholar who launched his love of ancient languages.",
