        "explanation": "Jefferson's polygraph was a copying machine, not a lie detector. Two connected arms held pens so that as he wrote, a second pen produced an identical copy. It let him keep records of nearly 19,000 letters. The device that encoded secret messages was his separate wheel cipher.",
